==Strategy==
The objective of this stage is to destroy the base within a time limit. Bring attack up, speed up, research up or worker up combos and unleash all your attackers.

Some Cats can make it by themselves, such as [[Ramen Cat]] or [[Crazed Axe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Dark Cat]], but it is recommended to also use other, stronger units when there is enough money, which could include: [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock & Pierre]] and a few others. You'll need an average of 50k DPS going around to make it in time.

==Trivia==
*This stage has the second highest [[Cat Energy|energy]] cost in the game, standing at 800, and the highest XP drop in [[Stories of Legend]] overall.
*The enemy base in this stage has the highest amount of health in the game, excluding invincible bases such as the [[Dummy (Enemy Base)|Dummy]].
*The stage's name is a likely reference to how the name of the chapter is false, as the true Stories of Legend ending, [[Eldritch Forces]], lies in the following chapter, [[Laboratory of Relics]].
*Despite being seemingly and likely meant to be unsurvivable, it is possible to beat the rush of Doge variants, although that typically requires near-constant debuffing attacks from various Uber Rare Cats.
*This is one of the only stages in the game that has a chance of rewarding a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], the others being [[Villains Jungle]], [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Aku Altar's Seal]], [[Reign of the Ape Lord]], [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] and [[Birth of True Man]].

